ivy-dev: quick sync: we need a final decision on fetch handling in the JS SDK. options: 1) require undici, 2) optionalDependency, 3) leave out and doc + runtime-detect. thoughts?

omar-platform: prefer runtime-detect + docs. Edge-first users must not pull undici into bundles. dynamic import undici only in Node runtimes.

lee-qa: agreement but add tests: Node(without undici), Node(with undici), Bun, Cloudflare Workers. catch streaming/response.body differences.

zhen-docs: also need clear docs for Next.js users (edge vs server), and warnings about common bundler polyfills (webpack/vite). many users hit that.

ivy-dev: prototype pattern:
```js
export function fetchSync() {
  return typeof globalThis.fetch === 'function' ? globalThis.fetch : null;
}
export async function fetchAsync() {
  const f = fetchSync();
  if (f) return f;
  const m = await import('undici');
  return m.fetch;
}
```
this avoids top-level await and keeps edge bundles clean.

omar-platform: nice. packaging note: if we list undici as optionalDependency npm will still download it for users. that might be surprising. leaving it out and documenting `npm i undici` for Node <20 is cleaner.

pkg-bot: FYI optionalPeerDependency will surface warnings in npm unless the consumer installs it, optionalDependency will be installed by default. choose based on UX tradeoff.

lee-qa: typings: if our types reference DOM RequestInit/Response TS will force consumers to include lib: ["DOM"] which is annoying. we should ship minimal fetch types in the package and export a FetchLike type.

zhen-docs: propose a small "TS fix" snippet in FAQ: show how to add DOM to tsconfig or import our fetch-types for minimal typing. copy-paste reduces support load.

sam-eng: runtime nuance: Bun/Node behave slightly different for streaming and headers. our HTTP layer should accept: string/Buffer/ReadableStream/AsyncIterator and normalize. add adapters.

omar-platform: retry and auth: implement retries above the fetch layer so token refresh logic is identical whether using global fetch or undici. expose low-level agent options only when undici is present.

ivy-dev: decision candidates: A) runtime-detect + no undici in deps (docs show install step), B) include undici as optionalDependency, C) bundle a tiny polyfill (no). I'm leaning A.

lee-qa: A + CI matrix + types file + docs = ✅. ensure we include a clear error message when fetch missing with next steps.

pkg-bot: add CI job for Node 16/18/20 + Bun + Workers in the PR checklist.

zhen-docs: I'll draft the README section and Next.js/Vercel example. include pnpm note about hoisting and how that affects optional deps.

sam-eng: I'll implement fetchSync/fetchAsync, CJS require shim, and minimal fetch-types.d.ts. will include tests for normalization of body types.

omar-platform: ok thanks. final call: runtime-detect + no undici in package.json + docs and CI. please add a clear migration guide for folks on older Node versions.

imy-dev: thanks all — I'll open the PR with the adapter + docs and tag reviewers.
